        "original_id": "477c3f7e-3289-52cd-8a52-f3843b48b3b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Nasdaq, Inc.; Citrix Systems; International Securities Exchange Holdings, Inc.\n- People: Mark B. Templeton\n- Products/Systems: NASDAQ stock market\n- Places: Europe\n- Topics: Financial services; software; stock exchanges; virtualization; cloud computing\n\nFacts:\n- From 2001 to 2015, Mark B. Templeton was President and CEO of Citrix Systems, Inc.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. is an American multinational financial services corporation.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. owns and operates the NASDAQ stock market and is also listed on it.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. owns and operates eight European stock exchanges: Armenian, Copenhagen, Helsinki, Iceland, Riga, Stockholm, Tallinn, and NASDAQ OMX Vilnius.\n- International Securities Exchange Holdings, Inc. is a wholly owned subsidiary of Nasdaq, Inc.\n- Citrix Systems, Inc. is an American multinational software company.\n- Citrix Systems, Inc. provides server, application, and desktop virtualization, networking, software as a service, and cloud computing technologies.",
